[2026/05/15 20:28:51] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': ' You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI’d like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS,\nItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback:\nMovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your\nworking directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon\nand MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit\ninteractions. Here’s the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random\nseeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based\n80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a\nshort statistical analysis.', 'Previous (buggy) implementation': '```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport re\nimport json\nimport math\nimport time\nimport warnings\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy import stats\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\'ignore\')\n\n# LensKit imports\nfrom lenskit import batch, topn\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.knn import ItemItem\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import BiasedMF\nfrom lenskit import crossfold\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Configuration\n# -----------------------------\nSEEDS = [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]\nK_LIST = [1, 5, 10]\nMIN_CORE = 5\nTOP_N = 50\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    \'MovieLens100K\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': [], \'runs\': []},\n    \'AmazonVideoGames\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': [], \'runs\': []},\n    \'LastFM\': {\'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []}, \'predictions\': [], \'ground_truth\': [], \'runs\': []},\n}\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Data loading / preprocessing\n# -----------------------------\ndef load_movielens(path):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\', names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'], engine=\'python\')\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3].copy()\n    df = df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'timestamp\']]\n    return df\n\ndef load_amazon_vg(path):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path)\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols.get(\'reviewerid\', cols.get(\'user_id\', cols.get(\'user\')))\n    item_col = cols.get(\'asin\', cols.get(\'item_id\', cols.get(\'item\')))\n    rating_col = cols.get(\'overall\', cols.get(\'rating\', None))\n    time_col = cols.get(\'unixreviewtime\', cols.get(\'timestamp\', None))\n    if user_col is None or item_col is None or rating_col is None:\n        raise ValueError(\'Could not infer Amazon Video Games columns.\')\n    keep = [user_col, item_col, rating_col] + ([time_col] if time_col else [])\n    df = df[keep].copy()\n    df = df[df[rating_col] > 3].copy()\n    df = df.rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\'})\n    if time_col:\n        df = df.rename(columns={time_col: \'timestamp\'})\n    else:\n        df[\'timestamp\'] = np.arange(len(df))\n    return df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'timestamp\']]\n\ndef load_lastfm(path):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\', engine=\'python\')\n    # user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat typically has userID, artistID, tagID, timestamp\n    cols = [c.lower() for c in df.columns]\n    colmap = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = colmap.get(\'userid\', colmap.get(\'user_id\', df.columns[0]))\n    item_col = colmap.get(\'artistid\', colmap.get(\'item_id\', df.columns[1]))\n    time_col = colmap.get(\'timestamp\', df.columns[-1])\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col, time_col]].copy()\n    df = df.rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\', time_col: \'timestamp\'})\n    return df\n\ndef core_filter(df, min_core=5):\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        ucnt = df[\'user\'].value_counts()\n        icnt = df[\'item\'].value_counts()\n        keep = df[\'user\'].isin(ucnt[ucnt >= min_core].index) & df[\'item\'].isin(icnt[icnt >= min_core].index)\n        new_df = df[keep].copy()\n        if len(new_df) != len(df):\n            changed = True\n            df = new_df\n    return df\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Evaluation helpers\n# -----------------------------\ndef make_algo(name):\n    if name == \'ALS\':\n        return BiasedMF(features=50, iterations=15, reg=0.1, damping=0.0, random_state=42)\n    if name == \'ItemKNN\':\n        return ItemItem(nnbrs=100, min_nbrs=1, center=False, aggregate=\'sum\')\n    if name == \'Pop\':\n        return Popular()\n    raise ValueError(name)\n\n\ndef eval_one(train, test, algo, k_list=(1,5,10), top_n=50):\n    model = algo.fit(train)\n    recs = batch.recommend(model, test[\'user\'].unique(), n=top_n, candidates=None)\n    # LensKit recommendations have columns: user, item, score, rank\n    if recs is None or len(recs) == 0:\n        return {f\'precision@{k}\': np.nan for k in k_list} | {f\'ndcg@{k}\': np.nan for k in k_list}\n    # topn.ndcg/precision expect user recommendations and test items\n    out = {}\n    for k in k_list:\n        p = topn.precision(recs, test, k=k)\n        n = topn.ndcg(recs, test, k=k)\n        out[f\'precision@{k}\'] = float(p)\n        out[f\'ndcg@{k}\'] = float(n)\n    return out\n\n\ndef run_experiment(name, df):\n    rows = []\n    for seed in SEEDS:\n        splitter = crossfold.SampleFrac(0.2, seed=seed, disjoint=False)\n        for fold_idx, (train, test) in enumerate(splitter.split(df)):\n            train = train[[\'user\', \'item\', \'timestamp\']].copy() if \'timestamp\' in train.columns else train[[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\n            test = test[[\'user\', \'item\', \'timestamp\']].copy() if \'timestamp\' in test.columns else test[[\'user\', \'item\']].copy()\n            for algo_name in [\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\']:\n                algo = make_algo(algo_name)\n                metrics = eval_one(train, test, algo, K_LIST, TOP_N)\n                row = {\'dataset\': name, \'seed\': seed, \'fold\': fold_idx, \'algo\': algo_name}\n                row.update(metrics)\n                rows.append(row)\n                experiment_data[name][\'runs\'].append(row)\n                print(f"{name} | seed={seed} | {algo_name} | " + ", ".join([f"{k}={v:.4f}" for k,v in metrics.items()]))\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n# -----------------------------\n# Main\n# -----------------------------\npaths = {\n    \'MovieLens100K\': os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'u.data\'),\n    \'AmazonVideoGames\': os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'VideoGames.csv\'),\n    \'LastFM\': os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\'),\n}\nloaders = {\n    \'MovieLens100K\': load_movielens,\n    \'AmazonVideoGames\': load_amazon_vg,\n    \'LastFM\': load_lastfm,\n}\n\nall_results = []\nfor ds_name in [\'MovieLens100K\', \'AmazonVideoGames\', \'LastFM\']:\n    print(f\'\\n=== Loading {ds_name} ===\')\n    df = loaders[ds_name](paths[ds_name])\n    df = core_filter(df, MIN_CORE)\n    df = df.dropna().drop_duplicates(subset=[\'user\', \'item\'])\n    # Normalize IDs to strings to ensure consistent handling\n    df[\'user\'] = df[\'user\'].astype(str)\n    df[\'item\'] = df[\'item\'].astype(str)\n    print(f\'{ds_name}: {len(df):,} interactions, {df.user.nunique():,} users, {df.item.nunique():,} items after 5-core.\')\n    res = run_experiment(ds_name, df)\n    all_results.append(res)\n\nresults = pd.concat(all_results, ignore_index=True)\nresults.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'all_results.csv\'), index=False)\n\n# Aggregate and save plottable arrays\nsummary = results.groupby([\'dataset\', \'algo\']).agg([\'mean\', \'std\'])\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'), experiment_data)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'results_array.npy\'), results.to_records(index=False))\n\n# Print summary\nmetric_cols = [c for c in results.columns if \'@\' in c]\nprint(\'\\n=== Mean metrics across seeds ===\')\nfor ds in results[\'dataset\'].unique():\n    print(f\'\\nDataset: {ds}\')\n    sub = results[results[\'dataset\'] == ds]\n    for algo in [\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\']:\n        s = sub[sub[\'algo\'] == algo]\n        vals = s[metric_cols].mean()\n        print(algo + \': \' + \', \'.join([f\'{c}={vals[c]:.4f}\' for c in metric_cols]))\n\n# Simple paired statistical analysis across seeds: compare ALS vs ItemKNN and ALS vs Pop on averaged metric per seed\nprint(\'\\n=== Short statistical analysis (paired Wilcoxon on seed-averaged runs) ===\')\nfor ds in results[\'dataset\'].unique():\n    sub = results[results[\'dataset\'] == ds]\n    for metric in [\'ndcg@10\', \'precision@10\']:\n        pivot = sub.groupby([\'seed\', \'algo\'])[metric].mean().unstack(\'algo\')\n        for a, b in [(\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\'), (\'ALS\', \'Pop\'), (\'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\')]:\n            if a in pivot.columns and b in pivot.columns:\n                x = pivot[a].dropna()\n                y = pivot[b].dropna()\n                common = x.index.intersection(y.index)\n                if len(common) >= 3:\n                    stat, p = stats.wilcoxon(x.loc[common], y.loc[common], zero_method=\'wilcox\', alternative=\'two-sided\')\n                    diff = (x.loc[common] - y.loc[common]).mean()\n                    print(f\'{ds} | {metric} | {a} vs {b}: mean_diff={diff:.4f}, wilcoxon_p={p:.4g}, n={len(common)}\')\n\n# Visualization\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 2, figsize=(12, 14), constrained_layout=True)\nfor i, ds in enumerate(results[\'dataset\'].unique()):\n    sub = results[results[\'dataset\'] == ds]\n    for j, metric in enumerate([\'precision@10\', \'ndcg@10\']):\n        ax = axes[i, j]\n        grp = sub.groupby(\'algo\')[metric].agg([\'mean\', \'std\']).reindex([\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\'])\n        ax.bar(grp.index, grp[\'mean\'], yerr=grp[\'std\'].fillna(0), capsize=4)\n        ax.set_title(f\'{ds} - {metric}\')\n        ax.set_ylim(bottom=0)\n        ax.grid(axis=\'y\', alpha=0.3)\nplt.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, \'metric_comparison.png\'), dpi=160)\nplt.close(fig)\n\nprint(\'\\nSaved results to working directory:\', working_dir)\nprint(\'Done.\')\n```', 'Execution output': '```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File "C:\\Users\\lukas\\AutoRecLab_Team7\\treesearch\\interpreter.py", line 147, in _run_session\n    exec(compile(code, self.agent_file_name, "exec"), global_scope)\n  File "runfile.py", line 15, in <module>\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'matplotlib\'\nExecution time: 3 seconds seconds (time limit is an hour).\n```', 'Bug Analysis & Scoring': "\n                Bug Analysis:\n                Execution failed immediately with ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'matplotlib' during import, so none of the experimen