[2026/05/15 20:29:51] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': ' You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI’d like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS,\nItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback:\nMovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your\nworking directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon\nand MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit\ninteractions. Here’s the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random\nseeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based\n80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a\nshort statistical analysis.', 'Previous (buggy) implementation': '```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport time\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n\nimport lenskit as lk\nfrom lenskit import batch\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import BiasedMF\n\nnp.random.seed(42)\n\nDATA_FILES = {\n    \'MovieLens100K\': \'u.data\',\n    \'AmazonVideoGames\': \'VideoGames.csv\',\n    \'LastFM\': \'user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat\',\n}\nSEEDS = [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]\nKS = [1, 5, 10]\nALGS = [\'ALS\', \'ItemKNN\', \'Pop\']\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    d: {\n        \'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\n        \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\n        \'predictions\': [],\n        \'ground_truth\': [],\n        \'results\': [],\n    }\n    for d in DATA_FILES\n}\n\n\ndef _read_csv_flexible(path):\n    for kwargs in [\n        dict(sep=\',\', engine=\'python\'),\n        dict(sep=\'\\t\', engine=\'python\'),\n        dict(sep=\'::\', engine=\'python\'),\n        dict(delim_whitespace=True, engine=\'python\'),\n    ]:\n        try:\n            return pd.read_csv(path, **kwargs)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    raise ValueError(f\'Could not parse file: {path}\')\n\n\ndef load_movielens(path):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\t\', names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'ts\'], engine=\'python\')\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3].copy()\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\n    return df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']]\n\n\ndef load_amazon(path):\n    df = _read_csv_flexible(path)\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols.get(\'reviewerid\', cols.get(\'user_id\', list(df.columns)[0]))\n    item_col = cols.get(\'asin\', cols.get(\'item_id\', list(df.columns)[1]))\n    rating_col = cols.get(\'overall\', cols.get(\'rating\', None))\n    if rating_col is None:\n        raise ValueError(\'Could not infer rating column for AmazonVideoGames\')\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col, rating_col]].rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\', rating_col: \'rating\'})\n    df = df[df[\'rating\'] > 3].copy()\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\n    return df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']]\n\n\ndef load_lastfm(path):\n    df = _read_csv_flexible(path)\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols.get(\'user\', cols.get(\'userid\', list(df.columns)[0]))\n    item_col = cols.get(\'artistid\', cols.get(\'item\', list(df.columns)[1]))\n    df = df[[user_col, item_col]].rename(columns={user_col: \'user\', item_col: \'item\'})\n    df[\'rating\'] = 1.0\n    return df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']]\n\n\ndef core_filter(df, min_uc=5, min_ic=5):\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        ucnt = df.groupby(\'user\').size()\n        keep_u = ucnt[ucnt >= min_uc].index\n        df2 = df[df[\'user\'].isin(keep_u)]\n        icnt = df2.groupby(\'item\').size()\n        keep_i = icnt[icnt >= min_ic].index\n        df3 = df2[df2[\'item\'].isin(keep_i)]\n        if len(df3) != len(df):\n            changed = True\n        df = df3.reset_index(drop=True)\n    return df\n\n\ndef make_split(df, seed):\n    tr_rows, te_rows = [], []\n    for _, grp in df.groupby(\'user\'):\n        idx = grp.index.to_numpy()\n        if len(idx) < 2:\n            continue\n        tr_idx, te_idx = train_test_split(idx, test_size=0.2, random_state=seed)\n        tr_rows.append(df.loc[tr_idx])\n        te_rows.append(df.loc[te_idx])\n    train = pd.concat(tr_rows, ignore_index=True)\n    test = pd.concat(te_rows, ignore_index=True)\n    return train, test\n\n\ndef ensure_numeric_ids(train, test):\n    users = pd.Index(pd.concat([train[\'user\'], test[\'user\']]).unique())\n    items = pd.Index(pd.concat([train[\'item\'], test[\'item\']]).unique())\n    umap = {u: i for i, u in enumerate(users)}\n    imap = {i: j for j, i in enumerate(items)}\n    tr = train.copy()\n    te = test.copy()\n    tr[\'user\'] = tr[\'user\'].map(umap)\n    tr[\'item\'] = tr[\'item\'].map(imap)\n    te[\'user\'] = te[\'user\'].map(umap)\n    te[\'item\'] = te[\'item\'].map(imap)\n    return tr, te\n\n\ndef precision_ndcg(recs, truth, k):\n    truth = set(truth)\n    if not truth:\n        return np.nan, np.nan\n    recs = list(recs)[:k]\n    hits = [1 if i in truth else 0 for i in recs]\n    prec = sum(hits) / float(k)\n    dcg = sum(h / math.log2(i + 2) for i, h in enumerate(hits))\n    ideal = sum(1.0 / math.log2(i + 2) for i in range(min(len(truth), k)))\n    ndcg = dcg / ideal if ideal > 0 else np.nan\n    return prec, ndcg\n\n\ndef eval_ranking(model, train, test, k_list=(1, 5, 10)):\n    users = test[\'user\'].unique()\n    truth_by_user = test.groupby(\'user\')[\'item\'].apply(list).to_dict()\n    recs = batch.recommend(model, users, n=max(k_list), ratings=train)\n    out = []\n    for u in users:\n        ur = recs[recs[\'user\'] == u]\n        items = ur[\'item\'].tolist()\n        row = {\'user\': u}\n        for k in k_list:\n            p, n = precision_ndcg(items, truth_by_user.get(u, []), k)\n            row[f\'precision@{k}\'] = p\n            row[f\'ndcg@{k}\'] = n\n        out.append(row)\n    return pd.DataFrame(out)\n\n\ndef build_model(name):\n    if name == \'ALS\':\n        return BiasedMF(50, reg=0.1, iterations=10, method=\'als\')\n    if name == \'ItemKNN\':\n        return ItemItem(nnbrs=20, min_nbrs=1, feedback=\'implicit\')\n    if name == \'Pop\':\n        return Popular()\n    raise ValueError(name)\n\n\nall_summary = []\n\nfor dname, path in DATA_FILES.items():\n    if dname == \'MovieLens100K\':\n        df = load_movielens(path)\n    elif dname == \'AmazonVideoGames\':\n        df = load_amazon(path)\n    else:\n        df = load_lastfm(path)\n\n    df = core_filter(df, 5, 5)\n    print(f\'{dname}: {len(df)} interactions after 5-core filtering\')\n\n    for seed in SEEDS:\n        train, test = make_split(df, seed)\n        train, test = ensure_numeric_ids(train, test)\n\n        for alg in ALGS:\n            model = build_model(alg)\n            t0 = time.time()\n            model.fit(train)\n            fit_time = time.time() - t0\n\n            metrics_df = eval_ranking(model, train, test, KS)\n            row = {\'dataset\': dname, \'seed\': seed, \'algorithm\': alg, \'fit_time\': fit_time}\n            for k in KS:\n                row[f\'precision@{k}\'] = float(metrics_df[f\'precision@{k}\'].mean())\n                row[f\'ndcg@{k}\'] = float(metrics_df[f\'ndcg@{k}\'].mean())\n\n            all_summary.append(row)\n            experiment_data[dname][\'results\'].append(row)\n            experiment_data[dname][\'metrics\'][\'val\'].append([seed, alg, row[\'precision@1\'], row[\'precision@5\'], row[\'precision@10\'], row[\'ndcg@1\'], row[\'ndcg@5\'], row[\'ndcg@10\']])\n            experiment_data[dname][\'predictions\'].append(np.array([], dtype=object))\n            experiment_data[dname][\'ground_truth\'].append(np.array([], dtype=object))\n\n            print(\n                f"{dname} | seed={seed} | {alg} | " +\n                ", ".join([f\'P@{k}={row[f"precision@{k}"]:.4f}, nDCG@{k}={row[f"ndcg@{k}"]:.4f}\' for k in KS])\n            )\n\nsummary = pd.DataFrame(all_summary)\nsummary.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, \'summary_results.csv\'), index=False)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'), experiment_data)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'summary_array.npy\'), summary.to_numpy(dtype=object))\n\nprint(\'\\nAggregated results (mean ± std over 5 seeds):\')\nfor (d, a), grp in summary.groupby([\'dataset\', \'algorithm\']):\n    print(f\'\\n{d} / {a}\')\n    for k in KS:\n        p = grp[f\'precision@{k}\']\n        n = grp[f\'ndcg@{k}\']\n        print(f\'  P@{k}: {p.mean():.4f} ± {p.std(ddof=1):.4f} | nDCG@{k}: {n.mean():.4f} ± {n.std(ddof=1):.4f}\')\n\nprint(\'\\nShort statistical analysis (paired t-tests over seeds, metric=nDCG@10):\')\nfor d in summary[\'dataset\'].unique():\n    sub = summary[summary[\'dataset\'] == d]\n    pivot = sub.pivot(index=\'seed\', columns=\'algorithm\', values=\'ndcg@10\')\n    for a1, a2 in [(\