[2026/05/15 20:31:35] [DEBUG] isgsa.llm: prompt content: {'Introduction': 'You are an experienced recommender systems researcher. Your previous code for research experiment had a bug, so based on the information below, you should revise it in order to fix this bug. Your response should be an implementation outline in natural language, followed by a single markdown code block which implements the bugfix/solution.', 'Research task': ' You are an expert recommender systems research assistant who is looking to help the user with their requests.\nThe user has some idea and you want to conduct creative experiments to gain scientific insights.\nYour aim is to run experiments to gather sufficient results to report back to the user.\nThe idea is:\n\nI’d like to run an experiment to quantify how much data split random seeds affect recommender system accuracy. Please use LensKit 0.14.4 to test three algorithms: ALS,\nItemKNN, and Pop. Run this on the following three datasets with implicit feedback:\nMovieLens100K, Amazon Video Games, Last.FM. The raw files are stored in your\nworking directory with the filenames u.data, VideoGames.csv, user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat. First, preprocess all datasets with 5-core filtering. For the Amazon\nand MovieLens datasets, please also convert any ratings greater than 3 to implicit\ninteractions. Here’s the main experimental procedure: Generate 5 different random\nseeds for data splitting. For each algorithm, dataset, and seed, please do a user-based\n80/20 holdout split. Train all models using standard hyperparameters. For the analysis, I need you to measure nDCG@k and Precision@k for k=1, 5, 10 and conduct a\nshort statistical analysis.', 'Previous (buggy) implementation': "```python\nimport os\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), 'working')\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\nimport json\nimport time\nimport math\nimport warnings\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom scipy import stats\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\n# LensKit 0.14.4 imports\nfrom lenskit import batch\nfrom lenskit import topn\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.als import ImplicitMF\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.item_knn import ItemItem\nfrom lenskit.algorithms.basic import Popular\nfrom lenskit.metrics.topn import ndcg, precision\n\nexperiment_data = {\n    'ml100k': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n    'amazon_vg': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n    'lastfm': {'metrics': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'losses': {'train': [], 'val': []}, 'predictions': [], 'ground_truth': []},\n}\n\n\ndef load_movielens(path='u.data'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep='\\t', names=['user', 'item', 'rating', 'timestamp'])\n    df = df[df['rating'] > 3].copy()\n    df = df[['user', 'item', 'timestamp']]\n    df['rating'] = 1.0\n    return df\n\n\ndef load_amazon(path='VideoGames.csv'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path)\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols.get('reviewerid', cols.get('user_id', cols.get('user', None)))\n    item_col = cols.get('asin', cols.get('item_id', cols.get('item', None)))\n    rating_col = cols.get('overall', cols.get('rating', None))\n    time_col = cols.get('unixreviewtime', cols.get('timestamp', None))\n    if user_col is None or item_col is None or rating_col is None:\n        raise ValueError('Could not identify Amazon columns')\n    keep = [user_col, item_col, rating_col] + ([time_col] if time_col is not None else [])\n    df = df[keep].copy()\n    df = df[df[rating_col] > 3].copy()\n    out = pd.DataFrame({'user': df[user_col].astype(str), 'item': df[item_col].astype(str)})\n    out['timestamp'] = df[time_col] if time_col is not None else np.arange(len(out))\n    out['rating'] = 1.0\n    return out\n\n\ndef load_lastfm(path='user_taggedartists-timestamps.dat'):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path, sep='\\t')\n    cols = {c.lower(): c for c in df.columns}\n    user_col = cols.get('userID'.lower(), cols.get('user_id', cols.get('user', None)))\n    item_col = cols.get('artistID'.lower(), cols.get('artist_id', cols.get('item', None)))\n    time_col = cols.get('timestamp', cols.get('time', None))\n    if user_col is None or item_col is None:\n        raise ValueError('Could not identify LastFM columns')\n    out = pd.DataFrame({'user': df[user_col].astype(str), 'item': df[item_col].astype(str)})\n    out['timestamp'] = df[time_col] if time_col is not None else np.arange(len(out))\n    out['rating'] = 1.0\n    return out\n\n\ndef core_filter(df, user_col='user', item_col='item', min_uc=5, min_ic=5):\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        ucnt = df.groupby(user_col).size()\n        keep_u = ucnt[ucnt >= min_uc].index\n        new_df = df[df[user_col].isin(keep_u)]\n        if len(new_df) != len(df):\n            changed = True\n        df = new_df\n        icnt = df.groupby(item_col).size()\n        keep_i = icnt[icnt >= min_ic].index\n        new_df = df[df[item_col].isin(keep_i)]\n        if len(new_df) != len(df):\n            changed = True\n        df = new_df\n    return df.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n\ndef split_user_holdout(df, seed, test_frac=0.2):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    train_rows = []\n    test_rows = []\n    for uid, grp in df.groupby('user'):\n        idx = grp.index.to_numpy()\n        n_test = max(1, int(np.floor(len(idx) * test_frac)))\n        perm = rng.permutation(idx)\n        test_idx = perm[:n_test]\n        train_idx = perm[n_test:]\n        if len(train_idx) == 0:\n            train_idx = test_idx[:1]\n            test_idx = test_idx[1:]\n        train_rows.append(df.loc[train_idx])\n        if len(test_idx) > 0:\n            test_rows.append(df.loc[test_idx])\n    train = pd.concat(train_rows, ignore_index=True)\n    test = pd.concat(test_rows, ignore_index=True) if test_rows else df.iloc[:0].copy()\n    return train, test\n\n\ndef evaluate_recommender(model, train, test, k_values=(1, 5, 10)):\n    test_users = test['user'].unique()\n    recs = batch.recommend(model, test_users, n=max(k_values), candidates=None)\n    recs = recs.rename(columns={'rank': 'rank', 'score': 'score'}) if 'rank' in recs.columns else recs\n    truth = test.groupby('user')['item'].apply(list).to_dict()\n    metrics = {}\n    for k in k_values:\n        try:\n            p = precision(recs, truth, k)\n            n = ndcg(recs, truth, k)\n        except Exception:\n            p = float('nan')\n            n = float('nan')\n        metrics[f'Precision@{k}'] = p\n        metrics[f'nDCG@{k}'] = n\n    return metrics, recs, truth\n\n\ndef build_model(name):\n    if name == 'ALS':\n        return ImplicitMF(features=50, iterations=10, reg=0.1, random_state=42)\n    if name == 'ItemKNN':\n        return ItemItem(nnbrs=100, min_nbrs=1)\n    if name == 'Pop':\n        return Popular()\n    raise ValueError(name)\n\n\ndef load_dataset(name):\n    if name == 'ml100k':\n        return load_movielens()\n    if name == 'amazon_vg':\n        return load_amazon()\n    if name == 'lastfm':\n        return load_lastfm()\n    raise ValueError(name)\n\n\ndatasets = ['ml100k', 'amazon_vg', 'lastfm']\nalgorithms = ['ALS', 'ItemKNN', 'Pop']\nseeds = [11, 22, 33, 44, 55]\nall_results = []\nstart_time = time.time()\n\nfor dname in datasets:\n    df = load_dataset(dname)\n    df = core_filter(df)\n    df = df[['user', 'item', 'timestamp', 'rating']].copy()\n    df['rating'] = 1.0\n    np.save(os.path.join(working_dir, f'{dname}_preprocessed.npy'), df.to_records(index=False))\n    for seed in seeds:\n        train, test = split_user_holdout(df, seed)\n        for alg in algorithms:\n            model = build_model(alg)\n            model.fit(train[['user', 'item', 'rating']])\n            metrics, recs, truth = evaluate_recommender(model, train, test)\n            row = {'dataset': dname, 'seed': seed, 'algorithm': alg, **metrics}\n            all_results.append(row)\n            experiment_data[dname]['metrics']['val'].append([seed, alg] + [metrics[f'Precision@{k}'] for k in [1,5,10]] + [metrics[f'nDCG@{k}'] for k in [1,5,10]])\n            experiment_data[dname]['predictions'].append(recs.head(1000).to_records(index=False))\n            experiment_data[dname]['ground_truth'].append(pd.DataFrame({'user': list(truth.keys()), 'items': list(truth.values())}).to_records(index=False))\n            print(f'{dname} seed={seed} alg={alg} ' + ' '.join([f'{k}={v:.4f}' for k, v in metrics.items()]))\n\nresults_df = pd.DataFrame(all_results)\nresults_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'all_results.csv'), index=False)\n\nsummary = results_df.groupby(['dataset', 'algorithm']).agg(['mean', 'std'])\nprint('\\nSummary by dataset/algorithm:')\nprint(summary)\n\n# Simple statistical analysis: pairwise paired t-tests across seeds within each dataset/metric\nanalysis_rows = []\nfor dname in datasets:\n    sub = results_df[results_df['dataset'] == dname]\n    for metric in [f'Precision@{k}' for k in [1,5,10]] + [f'nDCG@{k}' for k in [1,5,10]]:\n        piv = sub.pivot(index='seed', columns='algorithm', values=metric)\n        for a1, a2 in [('ALS', 'ItemKNN'), ('ALS', 'Pop'), ('ItemKNN', 'Pop')]:\n            x = piv[a1].to_numpy(); y = piv[a2].to_numpy()\n            if np.all(np.isfinite(x)) and np.all(np.isfinite(y)) and len(x) > 1:\n                t, p = stats.ttest_rel(x, y)\n            else:\n                t, p = np.nan, np.nan\n            analysis_rows.append([dname, metric, a1, a2, t, p, float(np.mean(x - y))])\nanalysis_df = pd.DataFrame(analysis_rows, columns=['dataset', 'metric', 'alg1', 'alg2', 't_stat', 'p_value', 'mean_diff'])\nanalysis_df.to_csv(os.path.join(working_dir, 'statistical_analysis.csv'), index=False)\nprint('\\nStatistical analysis (paired t-tests across seeds):')\nprint(analysis_df)\n\n# Save experiment data\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'experiment_data.npy'), experiment_data)\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'results_array.npy'), results_df.to_records(index=False))\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, 'analysis_array.npy'), analysis_df.to_records(index=False))\n\n# Visualization\nfor dname in datasets:\n    sub = results_df[results_df['dataset'] == dname]\n    fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(14, 7), constrained_layout=True)\n    metrics = [f'Precision@{k}' for k in [1,5,10]] + [f'nDCG@{k}' for k in [1,5,10]]\n    for ax, metric in zip(axes.flat, metrics):\n        data = [sub[sub['algorithm'] == alg][metric].values for alg in algorithms]\n        ax.boxplot(data, labels=algorithms)\n        ax.set_title(metric)\n        ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n    fig.suptitle(f'{dname} split-seed sensitivity')\n    fig.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, f'{dname}_seed_sensitivity.png'), dpi=150)\n    plt.close(fig)\n\nprint(f'Finished in {time.time() - start_time:.1f}s')\n\n```", 'Execution output': '```\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File "C:\\Users\\lukas\\AutoRecLab_Team7\\treesearch\\interpreter.py", line 147, in _run_session\n    exec(compile(code, self.agent_file_name, "exec"), global_scope)\n  File "runfile.py", line 14, in <module>\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'matplotlib\'\nExecution time: a moment seconds (time limit is an hour).\n```', 'Bug Analysis & Scoring': "\n                Bug Analysis:\n                The script failed immediately due to a missing dependency: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'matplotlib'` when importing `matplotlib.pyplot`. Because execution stops at import time, none of the LensKit experiments, preprocessing, metrics, or statistical analyses were run. To fix this, install matplotlib in the environment (or remove/guard the plotting section), then rerun the script. After that, verify the LensKit API calls and dataset loaders if additional issues appear.\n\n                This i